    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Borthwick overhauls England for Japan, with Ojomoh and Pollock starting",
          "body": "England named a much-changed side on Friday for Saturday's Japan match at Twickenham, with Steve Borthwick making ten personnel and two positional changes from the team that beat Australia 45-22. Max Ojomoh returns at 12 in his first England appearance since man of the match against Argentina a year ago, and Henry Pollock, who scored twice off the bench against Australia, starts at No. 8. Guardian rugby writer Robert Kitson called it a \"use-it-or-lose-it\" selection for players eyeing next year's World Cup in Australia."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat South Africa 21-19, ending home losing streak to Springboks",
          "body": "Argentina beat Italy 19-14. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon and Rob Valetini for Scotland."
