        "referee": "Pierre Brousset"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "Guardian Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Match result",
          "heading": "Antoine Dupont's France hold on to beat South Africa 21-19",
          "body": "Friday's Nations Championship thriller at Stade de France ended a five-match losing run against the Springboks on home soil. Injuries to fly-halves Matthieu Jalibert, Romain Ntamack and Antoine Hastoy left France coach Fabien Galthie with little option but to pick captain Antoine Dupont in the 10 shirt, although he played at scrum-half. Théo Attissogbe, Aaron Grandidier-Nkanang and Louis Bielle-Biarrey scored in a frantic first half, and Dupont was named player of the match. The win leaves France six points clear at the top of the northern hemisphere standings."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Argentina beat Italy 19-14",
          "body": "Borthwick overhauls England for Japan, Ojomoh and Pollock start. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon and Rob Valetini for Scotland."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-15",
      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Dan Sheehan and Sean Jansen injuries force changes to Ireland's XV against Fiji",
          "body": "Ireland head coach Andy Farrell made seven changes for Saturday's Nations Championship match against Fiji at the Aviva Stadium, two of them forced by injuries to Dan Sheehan and Sean Jansen. Jamison Gibson-Park is restored to the starting XV, while Joe McCarthy and Hugo Keenan were rested from the match-day 23. The replacements are James Ryan and Tommy O'Brien, and Farrell wants a bonus-point win to build momentum before South Africa visit Dublin next weekend."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "France beat South Africa 21-19, ending home losing streak to Springboks",
          "body": "Argentina beat Italy 19-14. Borthwick overhauls England for Japan, Ojomoh and Pollock start. Wallabies recall Carter Gordon and Rob Valetini for Scotland."
