      "edition": "Sunday 15 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Haka response",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy's Wales answer All Blacks haka with red-lit 'Dragon's Breath' display",
          "body": "Wales head coach Steve Tandy's side answered the All Blacks' haka before Saturday's Nations Championship match at the Principality Stadium. As the lights dimmed, New Zealand were picked out in a single spotlight; Wales were then bathed in deep red light and surrounded by smoke, a display the Welsh Rugby Union labelled the 'Dragon's Breath'. It recalled 1905, when Wales answered the haka with the Welsh National Anthem at Cardiff Arms Park. Fans online were quick to praise the lighting and choreography."
        },
        {
